      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the seven-digit number \\( 854n526 \\) divisible by 11, we use the rule for divisibility by 11. A number is divisible by 11 if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is a multiple of 11 (including 0).\n\nFor the number \\( 854n526 \\):\n- The digits in the odd positions are \\( 8, 4, 5, 6 \\).\n- The digits in the even positions are \\( 5, n, 2 \\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the digits in the odd positions:\n\\[ 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23. \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the digits in the even positions:\n\\[ 5 + n + 2 = 7 + n. \\]\n\nAccording to the rule for divisibility by 11, the difference between these two sums must be a multiple of 11:\n\\[ 23 - (7 + n) = 16 - n. \\]\nThis difference must be a multiple of 11. The possible values for \\( 16 - n \\) that are multiples of 11 are:\n\\[ 16 - n = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad 16 - n = -11, \\]\nor\n\\[ 16 - n = 11, \\quad 16 - n = 0, \\quad 16 - n = -11, \\quad 16 - n = 22. \\]\n\nSolving these equations:\n1. \\( 16 - n = 0 \\) gives \\( n = 16 \\).\n2. \\( 16 - n = -11 \\) gives \\( n = 27 \\).\n3. \\( 16 - n = 11 \\) gives \\( n = 5 \\).\n4. \\( 16 - n = 0 \\) gives \\( n = 16 \\).\n5. \\( 16 - n = -11 \\) gives \\( n = 27 \\).\n6. \\( 16 - n = 22 \\) gives \\( n = -6 \\) (which is not a valid digit).\n\nThus, the possible values for \\( n \\) are 16, 5, and 27. However, since \\( n \\) must be a single digit, the valid values are 16 and 5. We need to check which of these values makes the original number divisible by 11.\n\nFor \\( n = 5 \\):\nThe number is \\( 8545526 \\). The sum of the digits in the odd positions is \\( 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23 \\) and the sum of the digits in the even positions is \\( 5 + 5 + 2 = 12 \\). The difference is \\( 23 - 12 = 11 \\), which is a multiple of 11. Therefore, \\( n = 5 \\) works.\n\nFor \\( n = 16 \\):\nThe number is \\( 8541526 \\). The sum of the digits in the odd positions is \\( 8 + 4 + 5 + 6 = 23 \\) and the sum of the digits in the even positions is \\( 5 + 1 + 2 = 8 \\). The difference is \\( 23 - 8 = 15 \\), which is not a multiple of 11. Therefore, \\( n = 16 \\) does not work.\n\nThus, the only valid value for \\( n \\) is \\( 5 \\). The final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{5} \\]",
