      "text": "The digits of $854n526$ are $8,5,4,n,5,2,6$. According to the divisibility rule, if the difference between the sum of the digits in the odd positions and the sum of the digits in the even positions is divisible by $11$, \nthen the number is divisible by $11$. In this case, the sum of the digits in the odd positions is $8+4+5+6=23$, and the sum of the digits in the even positions is $5+n+2$. Therefore, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\n23 - (5 + n + 2) &= 14 - n \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nFor the number to be divisible by $11$, $14 - n$ must be divisible by $11$. Since $14$ is not divisible by $11$, the only possible value for $n$ is $2$. Therefore, the value of $n$ is $\\boxed{2}$.",
